  "2026-07-27T20:33:06.688Z","harness:codex","Exact-head Greptile P1 remediation: verified that runtime custom fields named cwd, path, or options could overwrite canonical MCP schema keys and move transport arguments into the mutation options bag. Runtime projection now leaves every existing canonical property intact; normalization derives reserved names from TOOL_SCHEMA_BASE and the canonical action schema before moving custom inputs. A real temporary tracker registers all three colliding fields and verifies stable workspace routing plus nested custom values. The finding was up-voted, answered inline, and resolved. Verification: focused runtime suite, full typechecks, ESLint, zero duplicates, strict static/docstring quality, contract drift, and 379-file/6,428-test coverage at 100% statements (44,601/44,601), branches (31,721/31,721), functions (9,138/9,138), and lines (43,318/43,318)."
